      "content": "A put/add followed by an increment of the same meta record loses the new revision stamp. `seen` retains the original, unstamped `write.value`, so the increment's later `put` overwrites the stamped record with a value whose `revision` is missing or stale, although `Committed.revisions` reports the new revision. Cache the stamped value for put/add writes (or preserve its stamp when resolving subsequent increments), and add a put-then-increment regression test.",
